From 57aec90ac57b4408ae7c5d1746bf2a693b5ed90e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: karfau <christian.bewernitz@bettermarks.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:32:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CVE-2026-83608: validate DocumentType.name under requireWellFormed (upstream 57aec90)
 serialization (GHSA-27p8-2357-5qqv)

Under `requireWellFormed`, `serializeToString` now validates a `DocumentType`
`name` against the anchored XML `Name` production (new `Name_exact` export in
`lib/grammar.js`) and throws `InvalidStateError` when it does not match, closing
the serializer name-injection gap that let a `>` or whitespace in the name break
out of the `<!DOCTYPE ...>` declaration. This matches the sibling
`publicId`/`systemId`/`internalSubset` checks and stays opt-in: the default
serialization path is byte-identical, emitting an ill-formed name verbatim. No
creation-time change is made; the `EntityReference`/attribute conventions are
unaffected. JSDoc and `index.d.ts` carry the new `@throws` and document the
writable `DocumentType.name` residual surface.

https://github.com/xmldom/xmldom/security/advisories/GHSA-27p8-2357-5qqv
